# Functions whose refusal a caller may not ignore, and the number of
# sites claiming a refusal cannot arise. Checked by
# tests/check-must-check.sh: the first list may grow and may not shrink.
#
# A function belongs here when it can decline to do what it was asked and
# the caller cannot tell from anything else -- an out-parameter left
# untouched, a store that did not land. It does not belong here merely
# for returning a status nobody happens to want.
#
# A name here may be a function pointer rather than a function. The
# refusal a caller has to answer is the same one, and the compiler holds
# a call through the pointer to answering it, so a function whose callers
# reach it through a member is only covered where that member carries the
# mark: the collector was called through two of them, and both discarded
# its answer while the function's own declaration said nothing.
#
# The count below the list is the size of the list. It is here so that
# retiring a name is two edits rather than one, and so that a set which
# shrank says so with a number that went down -- a diff dropping a name
# and its mark together otherwise reads as a tidy-up.

